Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:12:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader tables: c1_guard.py and cb_extent.py show their
 progress

After the compile, dmsh_build.py removes its progress file and runs
c1_guard.py and cb_extent.py over every shader of the library. The build
kept showing the compile's last count, "compiling: 99%, 42,848/42,848
shaders", for as long as they ran: over 20 minutes for Ocarina of Time on
Windows, where they ran on one core.

Their environment still names the progress file (DMSH_PROGRESS), so
table_progress.mapped runs the pool with imap, in the same order as map,
and writes each tool's step there at most every half second:
"final check: c1 reads" and "final check: uniform reads". ShaderWatch
shows a step other than the compile's as it is. Without DMSH_PROGRESS, or
with a pool that has no imap, it is the pool's map as before.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the build showed "compiling: 99%" for 20 minutes or more after the last shader, and players thought it had stopped
Issue: none yet (LosDaemons13/NX2Apple, a Windows build of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
